# These are consumed on Linux. CRLF would break shell scripts outright
# ("bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M") and stop the patches applying.
#
# The catch-all comes first so files with no extension are covered too:
# rootfs/usr/local/bin/w01-wifi and scripts/fel-emmc.py have no .sh suffix,
# and without this a clone on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the default there)
# checks them out with CRLF and they will not run.
*         text=auto eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.patch   text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
LICENSE   text eol=lf
*.bin     binary
*.png     binary
*.tar.gz  binary
